WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:01.934
 Good job, buddy.

00:00:02.001 --> 00:00:02.969
 You, too, brother.

00:00:03.035 --> 00:00:05.204
 Andy, Shane, congratulations.

00:00:05.271 --> 00:00:06.872
You've made it into
the final round.

00:00:06.939 --> 00:00:08.607
When you arrived here,
you used our tools

00:00:08.674 --> 00:00:12.011
and equipment to forge signature
blades of your own design.

00:00:12.078 --> 00:00:14.214
Now we're sending you
back to your home forges,

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.384
where you will recreate an
iconic blade from history.

00:00:20.686 --> 00:00:21.887
Butterfly swords.

00:00:21.954 --> 00:00:23.389
 Bad ass.

00:00:23.455 --> 00:00:25.091
 Butterfly sword,
or [non-english],,

00:00:25.157 --> 00:00:28.260
is a Chinese weapon developed
in the mid 19th century.

00:00:28.327 --> 00:00:30.029
Short and slim,
two of these blades

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:32.131
could be carried in
a single scabbard.

00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:34.867
Their small profile also
allowed them to be concealed

00:00:34.933 --> 00:00:36.569
in a boot, or sleep of a robe.

00:00:36.636 --> 00:00:39.939
The butterfly sword was forged
with a wide belly, which made

00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:42.242
it an ideal chopping weapon.

00:00:42.308 --> 00:00:44.443
Chinese militiamen
in the late 1830s

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:46.445
were outfitted with
butterfly swords,

00:00:46.512 --> 00:00:49.082
which allowed for deadly
close quarters combat.

00:00:49.149 --> 00:00:51.451
Due to its versatility,
it became a common weapon

00:00:51.517 --> 00:00:54.921
among many in China, including
sailors, private guards,

00:00:54.988 --> 00:00:56.088
and martial artists.

00:00:56.155 --> 00:00:57.623
These weapons were
also featured in one

00:00:57.657 --> 00:01:00.726
of the most popular kung
fu films of all time,

00:01:00.759 --> 00:01:03.763
"The 36th Chamber of Shaolin."

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:04.731
Good luck.

00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:05.732
We'll see you in five days.

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:09.702
 Day two of the challenge.

00:01:09.769 --> 00:01:11.137
I have a lot of goals today.

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:13.406 line:0%
The d guard is the main
focus this morning.

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:21.781
I think I'll still
round it a little bit,

00:01:21.847 --> 00:01:23.015
but that's the brass knuckle.

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:25.184
So we want that
to be able to put

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:26.619
an opponent out of commission.

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:28.754 line:0%
So after the d guards,
we'll have to cut

00:01:28.788 --> 00:01:30.156 line:7%
some wood for the handles.

00:01:30.223 --> 00:01:33.292 line:0%
African blackwood is a
very hard, dense wood.

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:36.028
It's hard to cut, it's
hard to drill a hole in,

00:01:36.061 --> 00:01:37.763
but it will take a nice finish.

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:39.298
I've got them dry assembled.

00:01:39.365 --> 00:01:40.800
I want to test these blades.

00:01:40.866 --> 00:01:43.002
I want to know they'll perform.

00:01:43.068 --> 00:01:44.436
The blade's hard.

00:01:44.503 --> 00:01:46.205
It was chipping a
little bit, because I

00:01:46.271 --> 00:01:49.675
had a pretty fine edge on it.

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:52.812
I'm going to have to
change the edge geometry.

00:01:52.878 --> 00:01:56.015 line:7%
Still a lot of work left to do.

00:01:56.048 --> 00:01:58.618 line:0%
 I need to make
myself a quench tank.

00:01:58.685 --> 00:02:02.221
It does not have to be pretty,
it just needs to hold the oil.

00:02:02.287 --> 00:02:03.989
This is for making horses poop.

00:02:04.056 --> 00:02:07.059
It's good for quenching
spring steel, too.

00:02:07.093 --> 00:02:10.130
[music playing]

00:02:10.963 --> 00:02:12.098
[bleep]

00:02:12.165 --> 00:02:14.801
Gee, this is really safe
next to a propane tank.

00:02:18.071 --> 00:02:19.672
Come on!

00:02:19.739 --> 00:02:21.440
Frickin' inferno here.

00:02:21.507 --> 00:02:24.576
That heat treat went
very well for me.

00:02:24.643 --> 00:02:25.311
Success.

00:02:25.378 --> 00:02:26.579
No cracks in those blades.

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:29.682
They're straight, they're
true, and they are hard.

00:02:33.385 --> 00:02:36.555
But I want to test the
strength of this blade.

00:02:36.589 --> 00:02:39.425
[chopping]

00:02:41.527 --> 00:02:43.630
Made very short work of that.

00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:46.665 line:0%
 It's time to quit fighting,
and just get her done.

00:02:46.732 --> 00:02:47.767
Day five.

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:49.635
I need to get the handles
sanded out and finished.

00:02:49.702 --> 00:02:52.938
I need to get the d guards
sanded out and finished,

00:02:53.005 --> 00:02:56.075
and I have to sharpen the blades
and do a little more testing.

00:02:56.109 --> 00:02:57.776 line:0%
So now what I'm working
on is the finial nut.

00:02:57.810 --> 00:03:01.781 line:0%
This will cinch everything
up tight when we glue it up.

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:04.350
Close only counts in
horseshoes and hand grenades.

00:03:04.417 --> 00:03:05.785
It's a constant battle.

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:11.624
So that's the first time
I've encountered that.

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:12.625
That was a mess.

00:03:12.691 --> 00:03:14.893
I'm feeling a whole lot
better now that they

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:16.563
are actually assembled.

00:03:18.998 --> 00:03:20.266 line:0%
 I'm going to build
the handles today.

00:03:20.299 --> 00:03:21.567
I'm going to fit everything up.

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:25.304
I need to make a pair
of nuts that I can use

00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:27.540
to cap the ends of the handle.

00:03:27.573 --> 00:03:29.108
It'll add a little
bit of counterweight,

00:03:29.174 --> 00:03:30.843
and it will also--

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:31.911
well, it'll just look cook.

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:34.480
Mother [bleep]!

00:03:34.513 --> 00:03:36.115
Argh!

00:03:36.182 --> 00:03:38.117
Holy [bleep].

00:03:38.151 --> 00:03:40.286
I knew that I would cut
myself on these blades

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:43.122
before I was done,
and sure enough,

00:03:43.189 --> 00:03:47.693
I cut my thumb pretty bad.

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:50.262
It's not a sword until
it's drawn blood,

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:56.168
so right now, painter's
tape and paper towels

00:03:56.202 --> 00:03:58.303
will have to do the trick.

00:03:58.370 --> 00:04:00.906
As you can see, my
shop is very sanitary,

00:04:00.973 --> 00:04:04.176
so I'm not worried about it.

00:04:04.209 --> 00:04:05.378
Where are my nuts?

00:04:07.546 --> 00:04:09.849
I can't have nuts
that are too big,

00:04:09.915 --> 00:04:12.351
and I can't have nuts
that are too small.

00:04:12.418 --> 00:04:14.987
My nuts need to be
just the right size.

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:17.323
Could have just slapped the
hardware store nut on there,

00:04:17.356 --> 00:04:20.826
but decided to make my own.

00:04:20.893 --> 00:04:23.162
Hopefully, this will be the
difference between bad ass

00:04:23.228 --> 00:04:24.597
and extra bad ass.

00:04:27.466 --> 00:04:29.702
Man, it's time
for a beer for me.

00:04:29.769 --> 00:04:31.470
 Bladesmiths, the
butterfly swords

00:04:31.537 --> 00:04:33.806
were designed to be short swords
because they were supposed

00:04:33.873 --> 00:04:36.275
to be maneuverable in
close quarter combat,

00:04:36.342 --> 00:04:37.410
and they were sharp.

00:04:37.476 --> 00:04:39.412
To test the sharpness
of your blade,

00:04:39.479 --> 00:04:40.813
I will attempt to
puncture, slash,

00:04:40.879 --> 00:04:44.583
and cut this trifecta of
sandbags, sugar cane, and rope.

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:46.185
Let's see how well
your blades do.

00:04:46.252 --> 00:04:47.186
Shane, you're up first.

00:04:47.253 --> 00:04:47.953
Are you ready?

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:48.788
 I am, sir.

00:04:48.855 --> 00:04:52.358
[music playing]

00:04:57.129 --> 00:04:58.364
 Nice.

00:04:58.398 --> 00:05:01.667
 Shane, your
blade moves nicely.

00:05:01.733 --> 00:05:05.204
It can definitely slash and
thrust through the sugar cane.

00:05:05.271 --> 00:05:06.506
It's sharp enough to cut.

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:08.140
At the same time,
on the rope, I can

00:05:08.206 --> 00:05:10.843
shield and then cut the rope.

00:05:10.877 --> 00:05:12.878
This, sir, will cut.

00:05:12.945 --> 00:05:13.979
Good job.

00:05:14.046 --> 00:05:15.013
 Thank you.

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:16.248
 Andy, you're up next.

00:05:16.282 --> 00:05:16.982
You ready?

00:05:17.049 --> 00:05:17.750
 I'm ready.

00:05:17.817 --> 00:05:19.018
 Let's do this.

00:05:19.085 --> 00:05:22.055
[music playing]

00:05:27.994 --> 00:05:28.861
 Great job.

00:05:28.894 --> 00:05:29.595
 Whoa.

00:05:29.662 --> 00:05:30.596
 Smoked 'em.

00:05:30.663 --> 00:05:32.965
 Well, Andy, definitely,
you've got a nice point

00:05:33.032 --> 00:05:34.934
to puncture and lacerate.

00:05:35.001 --> 00:05:38.604
On the sugar canes, nice
cut on my weaker side,

00:05:38.671 --> 00:05:40.573
and to use the
blade as a shield,

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:43.776
that feels good so I can
deliver my power thrust.

00:05:43.843 --> 00:05:46.411
And it's sharp.

00:05:46.445 --> 00:05:48.213
This, sir, will cut.

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:49.081
Good job.

00:05:49.148 --> 00:05:51.217
 Thank you.

00:05:51.283 --> 00:05:53.652
 Bladesmiths, this
is the kill test.

00:05:53.719 --> 00:05:55.254
The butterfly sword,
when sheathed,

00:05:55.321 --> 00:05:56.588
appears as one sword--

00:05:56.655 --> 00:05:59.425
but the minute you unsheath
it, you have two swords.

00:05:59.492 --> 00:06:01.694
To see how lethal your
butterfly swords are,

00:06:01.727 --> 00:06:04.730
I will deliver lethal blows
on these ballistic dummies.

00:06:04.797 --> 00:06:07.199
Let's see how much damage
your weapons can do.

00:06:07.266 --> 00:06:08.634
Shane, you're up first.

00:06:08.668 --> 00:06:09.267
You ready?

00:06:09.334 --> 00:06:10.169
 I'm ready.

00:06:10.203 --> 00:06:11.737
Let's do this.

00:06:11.804 --> 00:06:14.741
[music playing]

00:06:24.784 --> 00:06:25.618
 Nice.

00:06:25.685 --> 00:06:27.453
 Well, Shane, the
lacerations in here

00:06:27.486 --> 00:06:29.822
will go deep into the
bone and break it.

00:06:29.889 --> 00:06:31.390
At the same time,
when you thrust,

00:06:31.457 --> 00:06:33.959
it goes deep into the
bowels and cuts everything

00:06:34.026 --> 00:06:35.928
inside on its way out.

00:06:35.995 --> 00:06:38.364
This, sir, will kill.

00:06:38.431 --> 00:06:39.131
Great job.

00:06:39.198 --> 00:06:39.965
 Thank you.

00:06:40.032 --> 00:06:41.667
 Andy, you're up next.

00:06:41.734 --> 00:06:42.401
Ready?

00:06:42.468 --> 00:06:43.369
 Yes, sir.

00:06:43.436 --> 00:06:46.906
[music playing]

00:06:53.779 --> 00:06:56.516
 Andy, the design of
your blade lacerated

00:06:56.582 --> 00:06:59.485
this ballistic dummy deeply,
and that would puncture a lung.

00:06:59.551 --> 00:07:01.854
And when I thrust the
weapon, I completely

00:07:01.921 --> 00:07:03.622
disemboweled this dummy.

00:07:03.689 --> 00:07:05.991
This, sir, will kill.

00:07:06.058 --> 00:07:06.758
Great job.

00:07:06.825 --> 00:07:07.560
 Thank you.

00:07:09.795 --> 00:07:12.631
 Gentlemen, your final
test is the strength test.

00:07:12.664 --> 00:07:15.334
The butterfly swords
come from southern China.

00:07:15.368 --> 00:07:17.203
Now, though they were
used by the military,

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:19.405
primarily, they are
a civilian weapon.

00:07:19.471 --> 00:07:20.740
Now, to test the
strength of your blades,

00:07:20.807 --> 00:07:23.843
I'm going to take six
chops into this ice block.

00:07:23.909 --> 00:07:26.379
If they're strong enough,
that edge should hold up.

00:07:26.445 --> 00:07:27.646
Shane, you're up first.
Are you ready?

00:07:27.713 --> 00:07:28.981
- I'm ready.
- All right.

00:07:29.015 --> 00:07:29.782
Let's do this.

00:07:36.355 --> 00:07:38.991
 I've designed my blades
so that they will cut,

00:07:39.058 --> 00:07:40.559
they will chop bone--

00:07:40.625 --> 00:07:42.194
I'm pretty confident in them.

00:07:42.227 --> 00:07:44.730
 All right, Shane, well, your
edges held up beautifully.

00:07:44.797 --> 00:07:47.766
The weapon still feels nice and
tight, and well put together.

00:07:47.833 --> 00:07:49.668
What I do like is
the fact that I can

00:07:49.734 --> 00:07:51.604
hold this weapon in one hand.

00:07:51.671 --> 00:07:53.306
A question for you--

00:07:53.372 --> 00:07:55.407
you only sharpened
2/3 of that blade.

00:07:55.440 --> 00:07:56.508
Is there a reason?

00:07:56.575 --> 00:07:57.944
 The research that
I did said that only

00:07:58.010 --> 00:08:00.145
the bottom third of that
blade would not be sharpened,

00:08:00.212 --> 00:08:01.280
because of the monks--

00:08:01.313 --> 00:08:02.581
didn't want to kill somebody.

00:08:02.648 --> 00:08:04.116
They would want to thump
them and not kill a person.

00:08:04.182 --> 00:08:06.552
 I learned the same thing, but
it was when you reversed it,

00:08:06.619 --> 00:08:09.154
that that-- so you don't
put a finger on that edge

00:08:09.221 --> 00:08:10.889
when you reverse that blade.

00:08:10.923 --> 00:08:12.458
But nice design.

00:08:12.525 --> 00:08:13.459
Well done, sir.

00:08:13.526 --> 00:08:14.594
 Thank you, sir.

00:08:14.660 --> 00:08:16.095
 Andy, you're up.

00:08:16.162 --> 00:08:17.096
 Yes, sir.

00:08:17.163 --> 00:08:17.930
 OK.

00:08:17.997 --> 00:08:20.900
[music playing]

00:08:25.904 --> 00:08:26.839
A little wet.

00:08:31.210 --> 00:08:32.911
 Your edges feel great.

00:08:32.945 --> 00:08:33.879
Feel fine.

00:08:33.946 --> 00:08:36.047
I really like what you
did with the fullering.

00:08:36.114 --> 00:08:37.182
 Thank you.

00:08:37.249 --> 00:08:38.350
 A couple of things.

00:08:38.417 --> 00:08:40.452
The back arms are
just a little tight.

00:08:40.486 --> 00:08:42.488
I can't quite get
underneath that.

00:08:42.554 --> 00:08:44.290
I like what you did,
carrying them up there

00:08:44.323 --> 00:08:46.025
and putting that
detail on it, though.

00:08:46.091 --> 00:08:48.494
But the biggest
concern I have is I--

00:08:48.560 --> 00:08:52.598
I can't-- I can't hold that as--

00:08:52.632 --> 00:08:54.000
as one sword.

00:08:54.033 --> 00:08:57.003
I wouldn't be able to draw
that cleanly from the scabbard.

00:08:57.036 --> 00:09:01.473
Generally, though-- I mean,
they feel good in the hand.

00:09:01.507 --> 00:09:02.575
It's a good job.

00:09:02.641 --> 00:09:03.942
They held up well.

00:09:03.976 --> 00:09:04.476
 Thanks, Dave.

00:09:04.510 --> 00:09:05.611
 Nicely done.

00:09:05.677 --> 00:09:07.679
 Andy, Shane, the
judges have pored

00:09:07.746 --> 00:09:09.382
over the details
of your weapons,

00:09:09.448 --> 00:09:11.183
and they've made
their final decision.

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:14.654
Andy, Shane, you've both
done some outstanding work.

00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:17.422
In this competition, there can
only be one "Forged in Fire"

00:09:17.489 --> 00:09:19.391
champion.

00:09:19.458 --> 00:09:20.793
And that champion is--

00:09:25.131 --> 00:09:25.598
Shane.

00:09:25.665 --> 00:09:26.732
Congratulations.

00:09:26.799 --> 00:09:29.201
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:09:29.268 --> 00:09:30.235
Good job.

00:09:30.302 --> 00:09:31.336
 Thank you.

00:09:31.403 --> 00:09:34.339
 Congratulations, brother.

00:09:34.406 --> 00:09:35.974
 Well fought battle, bud.

00:09:36.041 --> 00:09:37.176
Absolutely.

00:09:37.209 --> 00:09:39.812
 Of course I would rather be
the one taking home $10,000,

00:09:39.878 --> 00:09:43.649
but I absolutely believe the
judges made the right decision.

00:09:43.683 --> 00:09:44.482
Congratulations.

00:09:44.549 --> 00:09:45.651
 Thank you.

00:09:45.684 --> 00:09:47.653
 Shane made a couple
of excellent blades,

00:09:47.720 --> 00:09:49.621
and he deserves it.

00:09:49.688 --> 00:09:51.791
This is Andy [inaudible],,
over and out.

00:09:51.824 --> 00:09:53.859
 Shane, congratulations,
you are the "Forged in Fire"

00:09:53.925 --> 00:09:58.030
champion, and will be
receiving a check for $10,000.

00:09:58.097 --> 00:09:59.097
Good job.

00:09:59.164 --> 00:10:00.032
 Thank you.

00:10:00.099 --> 00:10:01.166
I'm feeling wonderful.

00:10:01.233 --> 00:10:02.901
This is the moment
I've been waiting for.

00:10:02.968 --> 00:10:04.970
The journey is the
fun part, you know?

00:10:05.037 --> 00:10:05.938
I'm very happy.

00:10:05.971 --> 00:10:07.340
 So what are you gonna
do with the money?

00:10:07.406 --> 00:10:09.141
 I have a family
that's sacrificed a lot,

00:10:09.207 --> 00:10:12.578
so we'll have a family
council, and they will decide.

00:10:12.645 --> 00:10:14.847
 That's awesome.

